---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../layouts/Codeforge.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About MCP-B"
  description="MCP-B builds open-source WebMCP packages, browser tooling, and implementation guidance that help websites expose structured actions to AI agents."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="about-page__hero">
      <p class="about-page__eyebrow">About MCP-B</p>
      <h1>MCP-B builds WebMCP tools for websites and agents.</h1>
      <p>
        We help developers publish structured website actions that AI agents can discover and call
        without guessing their way through screenshots or click sequences.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-page__content">
      <section>
        <h2>What we build</h2>
        <p>
          MCP-B maintains open-source WebMCP runtimes, React bindings, browser transports, iframe
          bridges, and a local relay. The packages let teams add agent-facing tools to the web
          applications and workflows they already operate.
        </p>
        <p>
          Start with the <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/start-here/choose-your-path"
            >implementation guide</a
          >, browse the <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/packages">package reference</a>, or review the
          <a href="https://github.com/WebMCP-org/npm-packages">source on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where WebMCP fits</h2>
        <p>
          WebMCP is a W3C Community Group proposal for exposing structured page actions through the
          browser. MCP-B helped inspire the proposal and now provides implementation packages and
          bridges around it. The Community Group draft remains the authority for the proposed web
          API.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/explanation/what-is-webmcp">What is WebMCP?</a> or the
          <a href="https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/">Community Group draft</a> for the
          current boundary between the proposal and MCP-B.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who is behind MCP-B</h2>
        <p>
          MCP-B was founded by <a href="https://alexnahas.com/">Alex Nahas</a>. The project works in
          public through the <a href="https://github.com/WebMCP-org">WebMCP GitHub organization</a>
          and the <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/org/mcp-b">@mcp-b npm organization</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are evaluating WebMCP for a product or want help designing an agent-ready workflow,
          <a href="/contact/">book a call</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .about-page__hero {
    max-width: 58rem;
  }

  .about-page__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .about-page__hero h1 {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.96;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .about-page__hero > p:last-child {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-page__content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  .about-page__content section {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .about-page__content h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .about-page__content p {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .about-page__content a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .about-page__content {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
